This is the model that I ran. It has the maximal random effects structure a la "keep it maximal" (Barr et al., 2013):

library(brms)
attach(exp1_data)

fit_logistic <- brm(
  formula = response_vc ~ stim_length * ons_con * vowel + (1 + stim_length * ons_con * vowel | sub),
  data = exp1_data,
  family = bernoulli(link = "logit"),
  chains = 4, iter = 2000, warmup = 1000, cores = 4 # Recommended settings
)

# View results
summary(fit_logistic)

