🎯 Fixed Effects (Population-Level Effects)
Here are the key findings on the log-odds scale:
  Main Effects:
  
  Intercept = -0.18 (95% CI: -1.02, 0.67) - Baseline near chance when reference levels are long aspiration, /k/, vowel /a/
  stim_lengthshort = -1.41 (95% CI: -2.67, -0.22) - SHORT aspiration DECREASES voiced responses (credible effect - CI excludes 0)
ons_conp = -0.89 (95% CI: -1.89, 0.07) - /p/ tends to decrease voiced responses vs /k/ (marginal - CI barely includes 0)
vowele = -0.23 (95% CI: -1.18, 0.74) - No clear effect of /e/ vs /a/
  voweli = -0.72 (95% CI: -1.83, 0.31) - No clear effect of /i/ vs /a/
  
  Two-Way Interactions:
  
  stim_lengthshort:ons_conp = 1.13 (95% CI: -0.28, 2.59) - The effect of short aspiration is less negative for /p/ than /k/ (marginal)
stim_lengthshort:vowele = 0.08 (95% CI: -1.45, 1.54) - No interaction with /e/
  stim_lengthshort:voweli = 1.03 (95% CI: -0.59, 2.70) - Possible interaction with /i/ (marginal)
ons_conp:vowele = 1.96 (95% CI: 0.61, 3.38) - Strong interaction: /p/ + /e/ combination increases voiced responses
ons_conp:voweli = 1.24 (95% CI: -0.19, 2.73) - Possible /p/ + /i/ interaction (marginal)

